Zammad on FenrirOS
==================

Zammad lives in /opt/zammad (as upstream's packages), owned by the zammad
user. Three dinit services, none enabled: zammad-web (localhost:3000),
zammad-websocket (localhost:6042), zammad-worker. Commands run through
/usr/lib/zammad/run (it loads /etc/zammad/env). Nothing is set up for you.

Needs PostgreSQL and Valkey/Redis; Elasticsearch/OpenSearch is optional.

1. PostgreSQL: a role and database for Zammad (createuser zammad; createdb -O zammad zammad_production).
2. cp /usr/share/doc/zammad/database.yml.example /opt/zammad/config/database.yml
   (owned by zammad) and fill in the credentials.
3. /etc/zammad/env: REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379 (and anything else).
4. As zammad: /usr/lib/zammad/run bundle exec rake db:create db:migrate db:seed
5. nginx: /usr/share/doc/zammad/nginx-zammad.conf; enable nginx and the three
   services (dinitctl enable zammad-web ...), then open the site and create
   the first administrator there.
